    'kr.dd.note': `Kim Jeong-ho's Daedongyeojido (1861), the copy held by Seoul National University's Kyujanggak (Treasure no. 850-3); image from Wikimedia Commons (public domain). The old map has no grid, so the area shown is estimated by aligning it with today's coastline and may be off by ten-odd kilometres at the edges.`,
    'kr.sul.h': `Traditional liquor`, 'kr.sul.origin': `listed by place of origin`, 'kr.sul.src': `Only liquors on South Korea's provincial or national intangible-heritage lists or its Food Master register are included (source: Korean Wikipedia); one that originated in the North and is now made in the South is listed where it came from. No verifiable entries yet for other Northern regions.`,
