    'kr.era.joseon': `Joseon`, 'kr.era.joseon.p': `1392–1897`, 'kr.era.modern': `1897–1945`, 'kr.era.modern.p': `Empire & colony`, 'kr.era.today': `Since 1945`, 'kr.era.today.p': `1945–`, 'kr.st.seat': `Seat`,
    'kr.e.cap.samguk': `Sketch: the Three Kingdoms and Gaya around 500 CE, inferred from the origins of Silla's nine provinces — Silla set up Han, Sak and Myeong in former Goguryeo land and Ung, Jeon and Mu in former Baekje land; Gang province and Geumgwan (Gimhae) were the old Gaya states. When the Yeongsan River basin came under Baekje is still debated. Dots mark the capitals of the time.`, 'kr.e.samguk': `Three Kingdoms`, 'kr.e.samguk.s': `c. 500`, 'kr.e.samguk.tamna': `Tamna`, 'kr.e.samguk.out': `Other`, 'kr.s.samguk.pyongyang': `Pyongyang (Goguryeo)`, 'kr.s.samguk.ungjin': `Ungjin (Baekje)`, 'kr.s.samguk.geumseong': `Geumseong (Silla)`, 'kr.s.samguk.daegaya': `Daegaya (Goryeong)`, 'kr.r.samguk': `Three Kingdoms (c. 500)`,
