    'kp.cap.pop': `Colored by population today (South: mostly 2018–2025 figures; North: 2008 census)`, 'kp.cap.hh': `Colored by households registered in the 1432 Sejong Sillok gazetteer (each county counted in the region of its seat today)`,
    'kp.cap.kyol': `Colored by registered farmland in 1432, in gyeol (a unit set by yield: a gyeol of good land is smaller than one of poor land)`, 'kp.cap.density': `Colored by population density today (people/km²)`,
    'kp.cap.rise': `Change from 1432 household rank to today's population rank`,
    'kp.note': `Households, people and farmland for 1432 come from the geography section of the Annals of King Sejong (original text via the National Institute of Korean History's Annals of the Joseon Dynasty site). Each county is counted in the region where its seat lies today, with subordinate counties following their main county, so totals are approximate. Head counts were heavily under-registered (the gazetteer itself says only one or two in ten were recorded), so households compare better. For the southern provinces, county totals match the gazetteer's provincial totals to within 10 households; Pyongan and Hamgil include garrisons founded after 1432 and do not match. Population today: Wikidata.`,
