    'kr.e.cap.silla': `Unified Silla's nine provinces and royal capital (8th c.), pieced together from the present-day locations listed for each county in the nine-province tables of the Korean Wikipedia: each county today goes to the province that names it most, and unlisted counties follow their neighbors, so borders are approximate. Dots mark provincial seats. The northern edge ran roughly from the Taedong River to Wonsan Bay.`,
    'kr.e.cap.goryeo': `Goryeo's five circuits, two frontiers and capital region (11th c.), pieced together from today's counties (approximate). Assignments follow the geography treatise of the Goryeosa; all 83 counties whose names survive today agree with it. The northern edge is the Cheolli Jangseong wall; Jeju became Tamna County only in 1105.`,
